<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's 1996 public sector deficit $5.9 bln.</title>
<headline>Argentina's 1996 public sector deficit $5.9 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's 1996 public sector deficit excluding income from privatizations was around $5.9 billion, up from a $2.6 billion shortfall in 1995, a senior government official said Tuesday.</p>
<p>This was just shy of a $6.0 billion deficit agreed upon with the International Monetary Fund, Economy Secretary Pablo Guidotti told reporters.</p>
